    "title": "Control Board 4b: the historian",
    "why": "decisions/0171 §6 and §14 (release 4's second half, the session manager's OK): each process's readings are kept over time so every process and system has a trend: its light (on change, at least hourly) and each hour's counts. Opened, a process or a system shows its last 24 hours, 7 days or 30 days as an inline SVG with its uptime (time working against time it should have been on). Raw readings are kept 30 days (a Thresholds setting), one row per reading per day for 400. Insights → Telemetry points to the board. The health report lists the unused tables and columns (names and sizes only) so they can be sorted for the Founder; Database updates says plainly there's nothing to press there (Jason, 2026-11-18).",
